+\subsection{Specialists: skills, tools, and the fan-out} \label{sec:roster}
+
+An ``agent'' in this system is a small, inspectable thing: a role
+contract, the skill documents it must read, and the tools it may command.
+The intelligence is rented from a frozen general model; the specialization
+is ours, and it lives entirely in that triple. Two readers open every unit
+of work. A \emph{Skill Reader} begins each step by reading the step's
+Skill Library document and defect ledger and returning the binding
+checklist for \emph{this} burst---the procedure is consumed structurally
+at every step, never trusted to the operator's momentum. A
+\emph{Dispatcher} classifies each task by the artifact classes it will
+produce (figures, numbers, catalog writes, code ports, stochastic
+products) and returns the roster that must run, in order; a plan in which
+a producer approves its own output is invalid by construction, and any
+required guard that does not yet exist is surfaced as declared debt
+rather than silently relied upon.
+
+Producers then fan out---the fitting engine over time bins, panel builders
+over models, harvest readers over the published literature---and their
+outputs converge on verifier gates, each a fresh-context agent with one
+duty (Table~\ref{tab:roster}): every figure passes a vision check before
+any human sees it; every printed number is recomputed from the run's own
+products; a sub-threshold model-selection margin is reported as a tie,
+never a winner; a stochastic product must rerun bit-identically from its
+recorded seed; a ported algorithm is guilty until numerically matched to
+its source; no row enters a committed catalog unscreened; nothing is
+re-derived that the project has already proven; and every incident is
+closed into a lesson, at the correct enforcement layer, in the same
+session that produced it. A verdict is bound to a content hash of the
+artifact it certifies and expires the moment that artifact changes.
+
+\begin{deluxetable*}{lll}
+\tablecaption{The specialist roster: single-purpose agents around the producers.\label{tab:roster}}
+\tablehead{\colhead{specialist} & \colhead{position} & \colhead{binding rule}}
+\startdata
+Skill Reader & opens every step & the procedure is read structurally each time, never recalled \\
+Dispatcher & task intake & a producer never schedules its own approval; missing guards are declared debt \\
+Figure Verifier & before any figure reaches a human & no exceptions; verdict bound to the image hash \\
+Numbers Verifier & before any document ships & a number that cannot be recomputed from products does not print \\
+Tie Reporter & any model-selection report & sub-threshold margins are ties; preference is never argmin alone \\
+Seed Auditor & any stochastic product & a rerun must reproduce bit-identically or the product is not a result \\
+Port Verifier & any ported algorithm & a port is guilty until numerically matched to its source \\
+Admission Gate & any catalog write & no unsanitized row enters a committed catalog \\
+Prior-Art Reader & before any re-derivation & what the project has proven is read, not re-derived \\
+Distiller & after any incident & an incident that ends without a lesson is unfinished \\
+\enddata
+\end{deluxetable*}
+
+The tools the producers command are domain instruments, not generic code:
+the adaptive binning engine (Bayesian blocks merged to a significance
+floor), the fitting engine of \S\ref{sec:fitstep} with its validity
+gates, a temporal chain (minimum-variability timescale, cross-correlation
+lag with its sign convention stated, pulse-shape fits), the $\nu F_\nu$
+panel builder, and the literature harvester with its convention ledger.
+What makes an agent a specialist is not that it can run a tool but that
+its skill document tells it how to \emph{interpret} the tool: which
+estimator label rides every timescale, which margin is evidence and which
+is a tie, which fitted parameter is meaningful only away from its bound,
+and which published value may be compared only after frame alignment.
+The assembly is the reverse of the fan-out: verified outputs are composed
+into the Burst Record, the burst's typed state advances only when the
+products on disk evidence it (\S\ref{sec:skeleton}), and the record
+closes against the known-results battery of \S\ref{sec:verify}.
