+\subsection{The operating skeleton} \label{sec:skeleton}
+
+The doctrine is enforced by machinery, not memory. Each burst occupies one
+of fourteen typed states\prov---from ingested through binned, fitted, and
+assembled to closed, plus one terminal failure state---and the state is
+\emph{derived from the products on disk at read time}, never asserted, so
+the system cannot claim progress it cannot evidence. Every failure is
+classified into one of six classes\prov{} (transient, structural, contract,
+ordering, silent, guard), and each class carries a mandated response: hold
+and resume; label and continue; stop; wait; demote and make permanently
+loud; or, for a failed checker, fix the checker and re-run everything it
+ever gated. The rule that generates the taxonomy: \emph{an error message
+is never a behavior}---printing a warning is not handling a failure.
+
+Institutional memory is a \emph{Requirements Register}: forty numbered
+requirements\prov{} (one retired), each row recording a needed guard or
+agent, the incident that revealed the need, and whether the guard is
+deployed or remains declared debt. The Dispatcher sweeps the Register at
+task intake, so a missing guard is a stated liability rather than a
+silent gap. Enforcement obeys a hierarchy---code over hook over artifact
+over agent over prose---and each rule is moved to the strongest layer that
+can hold it. Three repository-level hooks\prov{} currently enforce, in code, that
+no figure reaches the human without a hash-bound verifier verdict, that
+raw data cannot be overwritten, and that no producer runs without a
+dispatch plan.
+
+Finally, each Burst Record carries a live approval ledger, assembled only
+from stamps and products it can link---it never asserts what it cannot
+evidence---and approvals are \emph{revocable by machine}: when an
+upstream decision is amended, a cascade mechanically demotes every
+downstream approval that depended on it, and reinstatement requires a
+human ruling with evidence. Both directions have operated in production:
+the cascade exposed an approval that had been given in conversation but
+never stamped (recorded with the delay disclosed rather than back-dated),
+and a demoted binning approval was reinstated only on proof that the
+binning's reference detector was untouched by the amendment, its block
+table byte-identical\prov. A conformance gate for assembled reports has
+its contract written and its agent pending; consistent with the
+Register's own rule, we state it here as declared debt.
+
